F215 — SELF.u64._0 is refused; the same read through a copy is not

    error: unsupported member read [id(4).u64._0]

[class.temporary]/2: selecting a member of a class prvalue materializes a temporary, and the member
read happens against that temporary's address. The resolver had three special cases for that — an
inline struct method, an aggregate-returning helper, and calls spelled `qpi.*` — and `SELF` expands
to `id(CONTRACT_INDEX, 0, 0, 0)`, an ordinary functional-style construction, so it matched none of
them.

Adds the general case: a call whose callee resolves to an aggregate type is a construction, so let
emitAddress place it in scratch and resolve the member against that. The rule is the callee naming a
type, not a list of producers.

Measured: SelfWord both backends `29 29 1` — direct read, read through a copy, and equal. Suite 1085/0.

